      "storyText": "Earlier this year, my co-founder and I found ourselves frequently switching between different coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor) anytime we ran out of shaky usage limits or a newer, better model came out.<p>We became increasingly frustrated with having to re-explain our tasks, workflows, common mistake patterns, etc. anytime we switched agents. We found no good free alternatives out there, so we built our own and fully open-sourced it!<p>Beacon hooks into 20+ different agent harnesses, captures session telemetry (prompts, tool calls, command executions, etc) in one normalized format, and distills it into common patterns and repeatable workflows with a human-approval step. This compounded knowledge is then accessible to any future agent via skills &#x2F; MCP.<p>We believe your agent data is yours to own and should not be locked behind any frontier lab&#x27;s ecosystem or closed memory infrastructure. We built Beacon to make working across agents way more transparent and efficient.<p>Try it out and tell us what you think: https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;Asymptote-Labs&#x2F;agent-beacon",
