      "storyText": "For the past few months, I&#x27;ve been building a product &quot;Linden&quot;. Its a low latency deterministic layer for ai agents. Linden helps businesses verify AI-generated outputs before they lead to real-world actions. It evaluates AI outputs against expected schemas, trusted data, and business rules to determine whether an action should be allowed, flagged, regenerated, blocked, or sent for human review.<p>Linden helps businesses ensure their AI agents don&#x27;t just produce convincing answers — they make decisions that align with actual business requirements, verified information, and configured limits.<p>I have tried cold email outreach that didn&#x27;t work. Published a professional demo across multiple platforms, drove 0 signups. Now, i don&#x27;t know if I just built something that serves no purpose. However, when i was building this, i did a research, looked at a lot of articles talking about the same thing. If this problem exists, then why no one willing to try it out?",
